# SPIR-V Tools Notes

## What I was trying to do
Understand how SPIR-V gets validated, optimized, and disassembled.

## What I started with
- spirv-tools GitHub repo
- validator, optimizer, disassembler

## What each part does
- Validator: checks correctness
- Optimizer: rewrites instructions
- Disassembler: turns binary into readable text

## What happened
- The tools are modular and easy to use.
- Optimizer passes are powerful but confusing at first.

## What confused me
- SPIR-V is very strict.
- Some passes require specific capabilities.

## What I want to try next
- Run validator on my own shaders.
- Try optimization passes.
- Compare output with glslang.

## Random thoughts
SPIR-V Tools feel like the “lint + tuning” stage of GPU code.
